0..74 Comment "// The refusals of implicit parameters (#315): a call omitting an implicit"
75..142 Comment "// nothing determines, one whose only solution names a binder of an"
143..220 Comment "// argument\'s own lambda, a call whose argument and expected type disagree on"
221..297 Comment "// one (#1216), an implicit written among the parentheses, a resident naming"
298..370 Comment "// no implicit, a use standing as a value with an implicit unsupplied, a"
371..446 Comment "// supply standing as a value whose implicit follows an explicit parameter,"
447..497 Comment "// and a telescope whose types mention each other."
499..577 Comment "// `same`, the identity at a type supplied by name, `twice`, whose combination"
578..655 Comment "// is implicit, `chosen`, whose implicit\'s type names its explicit parameter,"
656..731 Comment "// and `konst`, whose implicit is the result type of the function it takes."
